# atlas-bootstrap — packages emerged inline, outside any phase array.
#
# This set exists entirely because of the package-sets model. Under the old bash-array model
# these four were installed by a bare `emerge --noreplace` in the middle of a
# phase and registered themselves in the world file, so nothing ever noticed
# they were undeclared. Once the world file is emptied and the sets become the
# only depclean roots, an undeclared package is a package `emerge --depclean`
# removes — and every one of these is load-bearing.
#
# Found 2026-08-05 by diffing world against the real array members. An earlier
# pass that grepped all of phases/ missed three of them, because a package
# named only in a *comment* counted as declared. If you add another inline
# emerge anywhere, it belongs here too.

# phases/10-packages.sh:94 — bootstrapped before the GURU overlay is enabled,
# because eselect-repository needs git to sync. Also the repo's own VCS.
dev-vcs/git

# phases/10-packages.sh:98 — enables the GURU overlay, which is where
# nerdfonts, sd, watchexec and mangowm come from. Remove this and roughly a
# dozen atoms in atlas-core stop resolving.
app-eselect/eselect-repository

# phases/20-flatpaks.sh:9 — the flatpak runtime itself. The flatpak phase
# installs applications *through* it, so it can never be one of them.
sys-apps/flatpak

# bin/setup-ly:59 — the display manager. NOT in atlas-core: the GURU ebuild
# needs a Manifest workaround, so installing it must stay an explicit,
# auditable step (see README). But it must be a depclean root regardless, or
# the first converged run removes the only way to log in graphically.
x11-misc/ly
